# Task: Create Service Blueprint

## When to Use

Trigger this rule via @-mention when mapping a complete user journey or feature flow across front-stage (user-visible) and back-stage (system-internal) touchpoints. Service blueprints are useful for understanding how multiple features connect end-to-end.

## Instructions

1. Read and use `templates/template-service-blueprint.md` as the document skeleton. Fill in every bracketed placeholder.
2. Read `docs/vision-and-product.md` to align the blueprint phases with the See -> Learn -> Act model.
3. Read `knowledge/personas.md` to ground the user actions in a specific persona's context.
4. Reference the relevant feature specs in `requirements/features/` for each phase of the blueprint.
5. Save the completed document to `docs/`.

## Naming Convention

`blueprint-[journey-name].md` (e.g., `blueprint-first-time-learner.md`, `blueprint-onboarding-to-lesson.md`)

## AI Source Prompt

Every generated document must retain the AI Source Prompt block at the top of the file, recording the prompt used, the date, and the rule name (`create-blueprint.mdc`).

## Quality Checklist

- Each phase must define User Actions, Front-stage Interactions, Back-stage Processes, and Support Processes.
- The Line of Visibility must clearly separate what the user sees from what happens behind the scenes.
- Pain Points must identify at least one friction point per phase with a proposed improvement.
- Cross-references to feature specs in `requirements/features/` should be included where a phase maps to a documented feature.
